  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing the Images**\n\nI\'m deep-diving into the user\'s images to deconstruct their desired React TypeScript application. I\'ve begun dissecting the \"Vanity - Marcas\" view, focusing on its header elements and the \"Marcas\" content. I\'m noting the specific visual components and functionality required to recreate this brand view faithfully. I\'m focusing on the component structure.\n\n\n**Detailing the Components**\n\nI\'ve moved on to meticulously documenting the \"Vanity - Marcas\" view. I\'m focusing on the subtitle, notification bell, and user avatar. Next, I\'m charting the tabs structure, including the \"Mis Marcas\" and \"A\303\261adir Marca\" options. I\'m taking notes on the featured brand editorial profile, including the large banner image, circular logo, badges, brand name, and quote. I\'m making sure to log all the specific action buttons, like \"Editar Marca\" and \"+ A\303\261adir Producto\". I\'ve reached the product display, specifically the cosmetics grid. I\'m itemizing all cosmetic items in their two-column layout. I\'m documenting all the attributes of the products within the grid.\n\n\n**Cataloging the Carousel**\n\nI\'m now detailing the horizontal carousel, \"Otras marcas en tu tocador\", including the brand cards. I\'ve noted Dior, Tilbury, Fenty, NARS, and Maybelline as example brands, plus a \"Registrar Marca\" option. I\'m also cataloging the \"+ Registrar nueva marca en mi tocador\" button. I\'m focused on capturing the modal bottom sheet for brand adding and editing.\n\nI\'m now cataloging the \"A\303\261adir Producto\" form screen. I\'m charting its components and fields, from the back button and header to the \"MI COLECCI\303\223N PERSONAL\" badge and image upload options. I\'m focusing on the input fields for brand, product, reference, category, and shade, including the color swatch picker. I\'m itemizing the extra fields. I\'ve identified the \"Guardar Producto\" and \"Cancelar\" buttons.\n\n\n**Charting the Screens**\n\nI\'m now detailing the \"Producto\" (product detail) screen, specifically focusing on the back button, vanity icon, product details header, and share/more buttons. I\'ve noted \"CAT\303\201LOGO PERSONAL\" and \"En uso\" status badges, along with the hero image and brand link. I\'m documenting the shade section, color swatches, heart button, and detailed cosmetic attributes: category, purchase date, PAO, location, and personal notes. I\'m noting the edit/delete options at the end. I\'ve now begun cataloging \"Mi Tocador\", focusing on its header elements and the data displays.\n\n\n\n"
