    thinking: "**Analyzing Data Model**\n\nI\'m currently reviewing the necessary data model derived from the user\'s provided images and prompt. I\'ve broken down the \"Marcas (Brands View)\" screen, which includes a header displaying brand count, \"Mis Marcas (8),\" along with \"A\303\261adir Marca\". The data for this view has a featured brand, like \"Rare Beauty,\" and I\'m noting the presence of a banner image, a logo insignia, and a descriptive label.\n\n\n**Reviewing Feature Details**\n\nI\'ve just added more detailed information around the \"Colecci\303\263n Activa\" tag and how its connected to the product grid for each brand. I\'ve also noted that the vanity main view (Mi Tocador) includes the greeting \"Hola, Sof\303\255a \342\234\250\", and has counts for both total products and products to be restocked, along with a search bar and category chips.\n\n\n**Examining Product Screen**\n\nI\'m now diving into the product detail screen\'s elements. I\'ve noted the back button, vanity icon, the screen title, share and options buttons, and the profile avatar at the top. The \"CAT\303\201LOGO PERSONAL\" badge is displayed. From here, I\'ll go into deeper detail on the state dropdown and product grid view.\n\n\n**Detailing Product Screens**\n\nI\'m now detailing the product screen, specifically the status dropdown with options like \"En uso\" and \"Agotado\". I\'ve also noted the large product photo with its finish badge and the brand link. The Shade section is also defined including its color swatches and the \"Tonos en tocador\" row. \"Detalles del Cosm\303\251tico\" contains various details such as date purchased, PAO, and location which are now defined, along with my notes section. Lastly, I\'ve noted the bottom action buttons for editing and deleting the product.\n\n\n\n**Defining Product Attributes**\n\nI\'m solidifying the data structure for new product creation, focusing on attributes like shade name, color swatches, status, and personal notes. I\'m now also looking into the \"Deseos/Favoritos\" and \"Perfil\" views. I\'m reviewing the structure for wishlist items and user profiles (with Google Auth/custom login) in detail. I\'m also confirming the Firestore data structure.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 8
      nanos: 144460476
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
