  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining Firestore Rules**\n\nI\'m currently crafting the `firestore.rules` file for Firebase integration. I\'ve noted the essential requirements: `rules_version = \'2\'`, a default deny rule, and am now focusing on global helper functions like `isValidId(id)`. I am ensuring proper structure.\n\n\n**Implementing Security Rules**\n\nI have formalized validation for ID strings, ensuring they are alphanumeric, underscore, or hyphen-only, and meet size constraints. I\'ve defined essential functions: `incoming()`, `existing()`, `isSignedIn()`, and `isOwner()`. Security rules are now being implemented for the `/brands/{brandId}` and `/products/{productId}` collections. These rules are tailored to enforce ownership checks, specifically targeting user ID based access control.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 1
      nanos: 562277178
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
